<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>News from Europe - Latest world headlines and daily news - France 24</title><subtitle type="html">FRANCE 24 explores events across Europe, including in the 27 member states of the European Union and the United Kingdom. Follow our on-the-ground reports, interviews and analyses of the events affecting social and political life on the Continent and Europe’s role in the world.</subtitle><id>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/rss</id><updated>2026-09-30T15:00:13Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/rss" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>Macron says UK’s return to EU would be ‘excellent news’</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:501e9890d0f2d096a0df59936a8d13ac7a0d1175f28d2e1b45332c8df9c12ec2</id><updated>2026-09-30T15:00:13Z</updated><published>2026-09-30T11:49:56Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260930-live-macron-sanchez-hold-joint-press-conference-during-french-president-s-spain-visit" /><summary type="html">Speaking alongside Spanish Prime Minister Pedro Sanchez on Wednesday, French President Emmanuel Macron said that it would be "a good decision" if the UK decided to rejoin the European Union. The two leaders met at the Moncloa Palace in Madrid on the second day of Macron's two-day state visit to Spain.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Live: Several people killed as Russia launches new round of strikes on Kyiv</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:cd1b2844993e084e775ed88ff9321c6a7ddb0fdd43b9e1f8519f37542dafe559</id><updated>2026-09-30T15:00:13Z</updated><published>2026-09-30T05:35:15Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20260930-live-several-people-killed-as-russia-launches-new-round-of-strikes-on-kyiv--16599397238f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260930-live-several-people-killed-as-russia-launches-new-round-of-strikes-on-kyiv" /><summary type="html">At least five people, including a 14-year old child, have died after Russia launched another round of strikes on Kyiv and its surrounding regions overnight to Wednesday, officials said. Several people were also wounded in the attacks. In Poland, two airports, in Lublin and Rzeszow, were briefly shut over “military aviation activity” during Russian attacks on Ukraine. Follow our liveblog for all the latest updates.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Mystery over UK airbase scare as police find petrol but no explosives</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:d24f898f5487722c901dff68674ca615cf1cd2fc46d9d0f91a58961d3f0f21f8</id><updated>2026-09-30T15:00:13Z</updated><published>2026-09-29T19:05:41Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20260929-mystery-over-uk-airbase-scare-as-police-find-quantity-of-petrol-but-no-explosives--1845b2e97bf4.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260929-mystery-over-uk-airbase-scare-as-police-find-quantity-of-petrol-but-no-explosives" /><summary type="html">Britain's counter-terrorism police said ​on Tuesday that no improvised explosive devices had been found as part of an ​investigation ‌into a suspected plot targeting ⁠a British airbase used by US forces to ‌strike Iran, deepening uncertainty over the incident a day after five UK-based suspects were released on bail.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Burnham sets out 'new path' for Britain, vows to seek consensus on ties with EU</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:0d92184e0d51ce2090898af277410c410b58d17bb7fcb4cefdfe92ef3a4b820e</id><updated>2026-09-30T15:00:13Z</updated><published>2026-09-29T17:54:41Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20260929-burnham-sets-out-new-path-for-britain-vows-to-seek-consensus-on-ties-with-eu--7d1bd2026ea1.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260929-burnham-sets-out-new-path-for-britain-vows-to-seek-consensus-on-ties-with-eu" /><summary type="html">UK Prime Minister Andy Burnham pledged Tuesday to give Britain "a new social contract for the 21st century", reform the country's electoral system and build consensus on a new relationship with the European Union as he set out a long-term vision to tackle the UK's woes in his first speech as leader at the annual Labour party conference.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>'Putin's goal is to prolong his power in Russia': Journalist Roman Badanin</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:999083c66e05d61daa428d7d997ef20a9ed1db02e93d12be1f0031d7a2cd2654</id><updated>2026-09-30T15:00:13Z</updated><published>2026-09-29T12:46:30Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/perspective/20260929-putin-s-goal-is-to-prolong-his-power-in-russia-journalist-roman-badanin--91a3d314be95.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/perspective/20260929-putin-s-goal-is-to-prolong-his-power-in-russia-journalist-roman-badanin" /><summary type="html">A journalist who has spent more than 20 years investigating Russian leader Vladimir Putin and who is recognised as perhaps Russia's finest investigative journalist has told FRANCE 24 that Putin's aim with the war in Ukraine is simply to prolong his power inside Russia. Roman Badanin has just published a book, "Le Tsar en personne" or "The Tsar in person" which delves into exactly how Putin's mind works. Badanin says Putin acts like a gang member, and his attitude is that "if you beat me, I will beat you even harder". The book is so far out in Russian and French, with an English version to follow. He spoke to us in Perspective.</summary><category term="Perspective" /></entry><entry><title>Russia strikes two Kyiv data centres, cargo vessels in the Black Sea</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:35bed545e522f22cb4937fb3368bfa170d8a2f61801583f4fdcd1a74536d4dcf</id><updated>2026-09-30T15:00:13Z</updated><published>2026-09-29T10:35:57Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20260929-russia-strikes-two-kyiv-data-centres-cargo-vessels-in-the-black-sea--a01e81e5bcd7.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260929-russia-strikes-two-kyiv-data-centres-cargo-vessels-in-the-black-sea" /><summary type="html">Ukrainian President Volodymyr Zelensky said Tuesday that Russia launched a wave of overnight strikes across Ukraine, hitting two foreign-flagged vessels in the Black Sea and targets in Kyiv. The strikes come as Russia ramps up its pressure campaign intended to make Ukraine buckle under near-constant bombardment of its capital and other cities.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Trump 'surprised' UK granted bail to suspects in alleged airbase terror plot</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:33cc1f26b873550cfac008e31f5d5e1460a095de75fe38e6c4acd7c43ac164fd</id><updated>2026-09-30T15:00:13Z</updated><published>2026-09-29T09:12:07Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20260929-trump-surprised-uk-granted-bail-to-suspects-alleged-airbase-terror-plot--d79f276d3721.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260929-trump-surprised-uk-granted-bail-to-suspects-alleged-airbase-terror-plot" /><summary type="html">US President Donald Trump said Monday he was “surprised” British police released on bail five men arrested on suspicion of a plot to attack a UK airbase. Trump added the case “might be” linked to Iran, since the base has been used by US bombers to target Iran since March.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>'Class sizes of more than 36 people': School protests continue in Paris and beyond</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:9ae6f4c7b914e069f430db55892548e8c364b4665e999f2985d115cdbb2e220c</id><updated>2026-09-30T15:00:13Z</updated><published>2026-09-29T07:59:43Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20260929-class-sizes-of-more-than-36-people-student-protests-continue-in-paris-and-beyond-1--b5e875098054.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260929-class-sizes-of-more-than-36-people-student-protests-continue-in-paris-and-beyond-1" /><summary type="html">Teenagers in France have been blockading their schools and demonstrating since last week to protest a string of grievances. Standing in front of the Lycée Hélène Boucher, FRANCE 24 journalist Antonia Kerrigan said students there said there were "class sizes of more than 36 people". Click on the video for more.</summary></entry><entry><title>87-year-old Spanish pensioner whose eviction sparked protests to return home</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:520874ea2675a1b2bfb5425417bc8383d665b910665f4de11566d39f90d9024c</id><updated>2026-09-30T15:00:13Z</updated><published>2026-09-28T22:34:14Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20260928-evicted-spanish-pensioner-to-return-home-after-housing-protest-deal-spain-madrid--1f3eaf89a642.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260928-evicted-spanish-pensioner-to-return-home-after-housing-protest-deal-spain-madrid" /><summary type="html">An 87-year-old Madrid pensioner whose eviction became a rallying point for Spain’s housing protests will be able to return home after reaching a deal with the property’s owners, her lawyer said Monday. The agreement comes as demonstrations across the country pile pressure on Prime Minister Pedro Sanchez’s government to address soaring rents, a shortage of affordable homes and weak tenant protections.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Expert says UK air base plot 'fits into a very intense pattern we've been seeing in past two months'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:fc357b3c8a3c31a9ae40b960a9d26c114a87ccc857f70350d9da62fc14ecb510</id><updated>2026-09-30T15:00:13Z</updated><published>2026-09-28T21:25:18Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/a-propos/20260928-expert-says-uk-airbase-plot-fits-into-a-very-intense-pattern-we-ve-been-seeing-in-past-two---1fae47fd2b44.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/a-propos/20260928-expert-says-uk-airbase-plot-fits-into-a-very-intense-pattern-we-ve-been-seeing-in-past-two-months" /><summary type="html">British police said on Monday that five men arrested near an air base used by the United States were released on bail, as officers probed whether a "foreign state" could be involved in a suspected bomb plot. Speaking with FRANCE 24's Monte Francis, Yan Saint-Pierre, CEO of Modern Security Consulting Group, explains that many of the hybrid warfare cases seen recently "involve local nationals, this is not about exporting terror", adding that foreign actors aim to have "as many layers as possible to complicate any investigation and accurate denunciation of culprits".</summary><category term="A propos" /></entry><entry><title>Expert says UK air base plot 'fits into a very intense pattern we've been seeing in past two months'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:280e9e11d95641d82d2968d544a6b75080a79363fd97f13894ffaf170ba3518b</id><updated>2026-09-30T15:00:13Z</updated><published>2026-09-28T21:23:39Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/expert-says-uk-airbase-plot-fits-into-a-very-intense-pattern-we-ve-been-seeing-in-past-two-months--4b79d9d157f0.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/expert-says-uk-airbase-plot-fits-into-a-very-intense-pattern-we-ve-been-seeing-in-past-two-months" /><summary type="html">British police said on Monday that five men arrested near an air base used by the United States were released on bail, as officers probed whether a "foreign state" could be involved in a suspected bomb plot. Speaking with FRANCE 24's Monte Francis, Yan Saint-Pierre, CEO of Modern Security Consulting Group, explains that many of the hybrid warfare cases seen recently "involve local nationals, this is not about exporting terror", adding that foreign actors aim to have "as many layers as possible to complicate any investigation and accurate denunciation of culprits".</summary></entry><entry><title>RAF Fairford: AI-enhanced photos of suspects fuel false claims about their religion</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:6edb4a0d957db9d36e4e04364a3b470b8c96d40e0db7fa967d7adcde70614d5d</id><updated>2026-09-30T15:00:13Z</updated><published>2026-09-28T20:55:42Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/raf-fairford-ai-enhanced-photos-of-suspects-fuel-false-claims-about-their-religion-1--bb298c51157b.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/raf-fairford-ai-enhanced-photos-of-suspects-fuel-false-claims-about-their-religion-1" /><summary type="html">Five men arrested over a suspected bomb plot at RAF Fairford have been released on bail as investigations continue. Meanwhile, AI-enhanced images purporting to show their faces have gone viral, with some users claiming this "proves" the men are Muslim. SynthID confirms the sharpened images were created using OpenAI tools, meaning the AI has suggested different facial features. UK police have not disclosed any names or religion, only that the men are all British nationals. Vedika Bahl explains.</summary><category term="Truth or Fake" /></entry><entry><title>Ukrainian arms producers warn competitive edge eroding due to stringent export licence rules</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e77a6ec220f68261d7ea626b3339d56f4f34a138791d9bfd0a62cf805a393337</id><updated>2026-09-30T15:00:13Z</updated><published>2026-09-28T19:28:26Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/ukrainian-arms-producers-warn-competitive-edge-eroding-due-to-stringent-export-licence-rules--7f0830981503.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/ukrainian-arms-producers-warn-competitive-edge-eroding-due-to-stringent-export-licence-rules" /><summary type="html">Russian drones struck Ukraine's National Academy of Sciences in the historic heart of Kyiv on Monday, in the latest deadly daytime attack on the capital. Volodymyr Zelensky has long been pleading with Ukraine’s allies for more military aid to fend off Russia. But Ukrainian weapons producers say the country could be bringing in significant revenue of its own, if only they were allowed to export their products. FRANCE 24's Gulliver Cragg reports from Kyiv.</summary></entry><entry><title>Leo the moderate? Pope in France defends EU values</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:5e6c4dbf8daab6dbe6462a56db10f0bd1d4253044ea9427e5e8d395c5526fe49</id><updated>2026-09-30T15:00:13Z</updated><published>2026-09-28T18:49:50Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/the-debate/20260928-leo-the-moderate-pope-in-france-defends-eu-values--553ee529b6c0.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/the-debate/20260928-leo-the-moderate-pope-in-france-defends-eu-values" /><summary type="html">There's a new pope in town and he's got very different ideas on what France's far right calls the defense of Christian civilisation. Leo XIV is concluding his trip to France in the eastern city of Metz, which is closely associated with a founding father of present-day European federalism, Robert Schuman. There, the head of the world's largest organised religion proudly stated that Europe's roots are Christian, dating back to the Romans, all the while hailing an EU model that transcends "us versus them" ideology and brushes aside "might is right" in favour of human rights and international law.</summary><category term="The Debate" /></entry><entry><title>Pope Leo wraps up France visit, urging Europe to help combat 'lies and deceit'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c9040f6523b24642e0c5a8ed168dc5dffeff96554c76b30db2efcd62000bdbb5</id><updated>2026-09-30T15:00:13Z</updated><published>2026-09-28T16:00:10Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20260928-pope-leo-wraps-up-france-visit-urging-europe-to-help-combat-lies-and-deceit--c97b9fde2aab.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260928-pope-leo-wraps-up-france-visit-urging-europe-to-help-combat-lies-and-deceit" /><summary type="html">Pope Leo XIV urged Europe on Monday to draw from its Christian roots and tradition of dialogue to counter the "uncivilised" relations and "desire for domination" driving today's wars, as he wrapped up a four-day state visit to France that leaned heavily into politics and drew huge crowds at every turn.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Hybrid warfare: The threat of Russia looms over the Mediterranean</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:9a2b92e8198ef84259af4b488ba94ada043591627f212da1ba313e79cb044e9d</id><updated>2026-09-30T15:00:13Z</updated><published>2026-09-28T15:39:45Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20260928-hybrid-warfare-the-threat-of-russia-looms-over-the-mediterranean--7fafa51823e1.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260928-hybrid-warfare-the-threat-of-russia-looms-over-the-mediterranean" /><summary type="html">The CIA has reportedly warned several countries that Russia is preparing to launch hybrid operations across the Mediterranean Sea. But is the risk real, or is it a form of cyber warfare?</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>UK police bail five men held over suspected bomb plot at US-run air base</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:81ed1e876907e498337d76e71cd15777a32b585dce2353787a3771bc3008ffc0</id><updated>2026-09-30T15:00:13Z</updated><published>2026-09-28T15:01:40Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20260928-five-men-arrested-suspected-bomb-plot-uk-air-base-to-be-released-on-bail-fairford--fb35ccbbe65d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260928-five-men-arrested-suspected-bomb-plot-uk-air-base-to-be-released-on-bail-fairford" /><summary type="html">British police said Monday that five men arrested on explosives and terror charges near a US-run air base in England were being released on bail but remained under investigation. Counter-terror detectives said they were investigating "multiple lines of inquiry", including whether there is a link to Iran.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Russian attacks kill eight in Ukraine after Moscow vows to continue war</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:224646d28e29e4c99235ea1dede3d6083a99a32097cab17a5513e599e59df0a5</id><updated>2026-09-30T15:00:13Z</updated><published>2026-09-27T21:55:28Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20260927-russian-strikes-kill-eight-ukraine-war-moscow--369b70639b79.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260927-russian-strikes-kill-eight-ukraine-war-moscow" /><summary type="html">Russian strikes killed eight people across Ukraine on Sunday, authorities said, a day after Moscow vowed to continue the war. Ukraine's President Volodymyr Zelensky said Russia had launched about 3,900 drones, aerial bombs and missiles over the past week. Kyiv accused Moscow of deliberately targeting civilians as winter approaches.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Serbian President Aleksandar Vucic resigns to run for prime minister in October elections</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:0342a19d976e9319bead911febcec820dc278a5ea9f46b07e14c805d1d67b0f1</id><updated>2026-09-30T15:00:13Z</updated><published>2026-09-27T18:17:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20260927-serbian-president-aleksandar-vucic-resigns-expected-to-run-for-prime-minister--44f496fa3711.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260927-serbian-president-aleksandar-vucic-resigns-expected-to-run-for-prime-minister" /><summary type="html">Serbian President Aleksandar Vucic stepped down as the country's head of state Sunday, paving the way for him to run as his right-wing populist Serbian Progressive Party's candidate for prime minister in the October parliamentary elections.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Non! Why the Swiss rejected stricter neutrality</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:611a725f8fe28ea7e63ed08d084b03272bd738521adf493cf22b831c4d43cd75</id><updated>2026-09-30T15:00:13Z</updated><published>2026-09-27T17:33:09Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/spotlight/20260927-non-why-the-swiss-rejected-stricter-neutrality--36da3bab7b90.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/spotlight/20260927-non-why-the-swiss-rejected-stricter-neutrality" /><summary type="html">A referendum has been held in Switzerland on whether Swiss neutrality should be more strictly enforced in the Constitution. Richard Werly, Europe correspondent for the Swiss publication Blick, tell us why the Swiss have voted "no".</summary><category term="Spotlight" /></entry><entry><title>First Protestant march in Catholic area in nearly 30 years</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:58659693c69906e08f9fe6f7ac06f11b07424bf1f5fad8faf32a0c833a87a4da</id><updated>2026-09-30T15:00:13Z</updated><published>2026-09-27T13:54:28Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/first-protestant-march-in-catholic-area-in-nearly-30-years--f8af8719a6be.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/first-protestant-march-in-catholic-area-in-nearly-30-years" /><summary type="html">Tensions are running high in Northern Ireland after the High Court in Belfast approved a controversial parade. Around 2,000 protesters have blocked the route into a Catholic area where the Protestant march was due to pass. It is the first time in nearly 30 years that the Orange Order has been allowed to march along this route, which was a notorious flashpoint before the 1998 Good Friday Agreement largely brought an end to the bloodshed of the Troubles. UK Prime Minister Andy Burnham has appealed for calm on all sides, saying he does not want to see Northern Ireland “go backwards.”</summary></entry><entry><title>UK police arrest 5 men, counter-terror squad probes ‘major incident’ near air base used by US forces</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:7bdcd9a4f65a8020ad1da2b446254f2a6b4a99f5419e4e83e9c9946bdd430b0d</id><updated>2026-09-30T15:00:13Z</updated><published>2026-09-27T09:05:06Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20260927-uk-police-evacuate-homes-near-air-base-used-by-us-arrest-men-on-suspected-explosives-offens--0f588bed1f6a.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260927-uk-police-evacuate-homes-near-air-base-used-by-us-arrest-men-on-suspected-explosives-offenses" /><summary type="html">British police said they had evacuated homes Sunday near the air base of Fairford in southwest England used by US air forces and arrested five men over suspected explosives offences. British counter-terrorism police are investigating the incident.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Northern Ireland court allows Orange Order march through Catholic area</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:5de192fd86a2520a124ade3dcef902fd02e2597cf6d1bd349d6184061d22f6e9</id><updated>2026-09-30T15:00:13Z</updated><published>2026-09-27T08:41:07Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/northern-ireland-court-allows-orange-order-march-through-catholic-area--cd2e81692b6c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/northern-ireland-court-allows-orange-order-march-through-catholic-area" /><summary type="html">A court in Northern Ireland has allowed a Protestant parade to proceed through a controversial route in a Catholic area for the first time in nearly 30 years. The legal dispute ended in the early hours of Sunday, with counterprotests now underway and police working to keep marchers and protesters apart. The Drumcree parade dispute dates back to the mid-1990s, when tensions over the route led to riots, roadblocks and murders, threatening Northern Ireland’s peace process. Hervé Amoric reports from Portadown.</summary></entry><entry><title>Switzerland votes on country's neutrality</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:02bf781a2e725fa848b713d205b7f116026441cf12d1df429dc8d748150f5c0c</id><updated>2026-09-30T15:00:13Z</updated><published>2026-09-27T08:36:49Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/switzerland-votes-on-country-s-neutrality--3dc1a1a4c6fc.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/switzerland-votes-on-country-s-neutrality" /><summary type="html">As other neutral countries such as Austria and Ireland increase defence spending and strengthen ties with NATO, Swiss voters are taking part in a referendum on whether to enshrine a stricter definition of the country’s centuries-old neutrality in the constitution. Switzerland has not fought a military conflict since neutrality was established in 1815, but some argue that measures such as sanctions can undermine that principle. The vote also raises questions about how neutrality can be maintained amid Europe’s changing security landscape, with Russia at war with Ukraine and the US putting pressure on traditional alliances such as NATO. Josh Vardey reports.</summary></entry><entry><title>Northern Ireland: Disputed parade set for flashpoint after nearly 30 years</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:14a086d15387b67f70d579eb6ed349a5653b2c59bc476ef076f36bbc2eba6432</id><updated>2026-09-30T15:00:13Z</updated><published>2026-09-27T08:33:22Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/northern-ireland-disputed-parade-set-for-flashpoint-after-nearly-30-years--a8b3f339a0fd.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/northern-ireland-disputed-parade-set-for-flashpoint-after-nearly-30-years" /><summary type="html">A court in Northern Ireland has allowed a Protestant parade to proceed through a controversial route in a Catholic area for the first time in nearly 30 years. The legal dispute ended in the early hours of Sunday, with counterprotests now underway and police working to keep marchers and protesters apart. The Drumcree parade dispute dates back to the mid-1990s, when tensions over the route led to riots, roadblocks and murders, threatening Northern Ireland’s peace process. Hervé Amoric reports from Portadown.</summary></entry><entry><title>‘Russian sleeper cell’: Can Germany’s far-right AfD be barred from sensitive intel?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a1e4f9ad451dc8b37ba2d2b7d42742fc418c429279c911f8641b2e1b6c3958dd</id><updated>2026-09-30T15:00:13Z</updated><published>2026-09-27T08:03:21Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20260927-russian-sleeper-cell-can-germany-far-right-afd-be-barred-from-sensitive-intelligence--5ad0a02478bb.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260927-russian-sleeper-cell-can-germany-far-right-afd-be-barred-from-sensitive-intelligence" /><summary type="html">The prospect of an AfD-led government in Germany’s Saxony-Anhalt has exacerbated long-standing fears that the far-right Russia-friendly party may gain access to sensitive information of interest to the Kremlin, fuelling debate as to whether and how it can be barred from classified intelligence.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Swiss reject plan to adopt stricter form of neutrality that would rule out NATO cooperation</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:be8081b32f180c7878fecc89c2456480a06e685ca1a4c704369bf6aaeba21735</id><updated>2026-09-30T15:00:13Z</updated><published>2026-09-27T05:52:08Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20260927-swiss-reject-plan-to-adopt-stricter-form-of-neutrality-that-would-rule-out-nato-cooperation--e98aeaafb123.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260927-swiss-reject-plan-to-adopt-stricter-form-of-neutrality-that-would-rule-out-nato-cooperation" /><summary type="html">Swiss voters on Sunday voted against a proposal that would have imposed a more restrictive form of neutrality on the Alpine country, preventing it from levelling sanctions without UN backing or joining military alliances except when under direct attack. Switzerland's centuries-long tradition of "armed neutrality" has not prevented the government from throwing its support behind EU sanctions on Russia following Moscow's invasion of Ukraine.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Maricarmen vs the 'vultures': A 'social tragedy' mobilising Spaniards</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:655b332f307c8b7a27c483449efad00285ff6a815d3094f903ed666f9abe4cba</id><updated>2026-09-30T15:00:13Z</updated><published>2026-09-26T18:03:40Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/spotlight/20260926-maricarmen-vs-the-vultures-a-social-tragedy-mobilising-spaniards--68b38ed468b2.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/spotlight/20260926-maricarmen-vs-the-vultures-a-social-tragedy-mobilising-spaniards" /><summary type="html">Protests are ongoing in Madrid right now, with many demonstrators holding signs and banners that read "Maricarmen vs the vultures", "Maricarmen, you are not alone", or "Ni una Maricarmen más", not one more Maricarmen.</summary><category term="Spotlight" /></entry><entry><title>Thousands march in Madrid to protest eviction of 87-year-old woman</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:912a644d3a4b362f4684e5264387fb723c41d528318df26352d995439abe08b2</id><updated>2026-09-30T15:00:13Z</updated><published>2026-09-26T17:04:06Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20260926-thousands-march-in-madrid-to-protest-eviction-of-87-year-old-woman--7fbee8e45e98.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260926-thousands-march-in-madrid-to-protest-eviction-of-87-year-old-woman" /><summary type="html">The eviction of 87-year-old Maricarmen Abascal on Wednesday sparked a thousands-strong protest in Madrid Saturday, with demonstrators demanding greater tenant protection. Widespread anger at rising housing costs have put pressure on Prime Minister Pedro Sanchez's government, which is expected to approve pro-tenant measures in its next cabinet meeting.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>At least 16 people killed as Russia and Ukraine trade deadly air strikes</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:18f155015b972fdb860e69107fe9855e7c2f7d1a7a111919fd5c51bb07e87318</id><updated>2026-09-30T15:00:13Z</updated><published>2026-09-26T15:40:10Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20260926-at-least-16-people-killed-as-russia-and-ukraine-trade-deadly-air-strikes--55f3b33690aa.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260926-at-least-16-people-killed-as-russia-and-ukraine-trade-deadly-air-strikes" /><summary type="html">At least 16 people were killed over the past 24 hours as Russia and Ukraine traded deadly drone and missile strikes, authorities from both countries said Saturday. The UN has warned of rising civilian deaths as Kyiv and Moscow ramp up long-range strikes on critical infrastructure.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry></feed>
